# 30825-30831 -- LAN server discovery (core/discovery.py, plugin/serverpicker.py).
# #30829 names manual entry rather than suggesting another go, and the wording
# is the protocol's, not politeness: a server answers the broadcast in
# milliseconds or not at all, so nothing is still on its way when the window
# closes, and the usual causes -- auto-discovery switched off, Docker bridge
# networking, another subnet, a host where something already holds UDP 7359 --
# no number of retries reaches. #30830 marks a row whose address did not
# answer and reads as a fragment after the address; #30831 is the same fact as
# a sentence, raised only if the user picks that row anyway. %s is the
# server's own name.
msgctxt "#30825"
msgid "Find servers on local network"
